Do not touch: `crates/engine/`, `crates/cards/`, `spec/`, `crates/ai/README.md`, `crates/ai/src/config.rs`, `crates/ai/src/reply.rs`, any patch fragment (an AI change is not a card change, so `classify --claims` needs none). No ruling: this is AI estimation, not a game rule. Governing spec: §6.1 (Rush lifts sickness for unit targets only, Charge for the hero too), §4.2 step 3 (the Taunt wall), §4.4 step 9 (Trample excess is a new damage instance), §9.9 (the lethal solver).

## Steps

**Trap, read first.** Do NOT take the flag from `has_attack`'s `can_attack(state, unit, &AttackTarget::Hero { .. })`, as the issue suggests. That call is false for every attacker a Taunt wall binds (`crates/engine/src/combat.rs`, `why_cannot_attack_in`, "a Taunt unit must be attacked first"). Every walled attacker would then add 0 once its Taunt fell. The flag has to mean "may hit the hero once no Taunt walls it". It mirrors the engine's own Rush check (`combat.rs` lines 466-471: `is_sick && !Charge` refuses the hero). An E35 restriction never bars the hero alone: `attack_restriction` on a hero checks only `cannot_attack`, which bars every target, so `has_attack` is already false.

